course: dictionary
lesson: 5244
title: Jitters and jitter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. Look at the words around it. «Two cans means twice the caffeine and more jitters and a bigger crash, not twice the fitness.» Here jitters are nervous, shaky feelings, because a bigger crash and more worry are unpleasant feelings.
explain: The word can also be a verb. To jitter means to make small, quick, shaky movements. In «caffeine more often brings jitters and worry», jitters sits next to worry, so it names a feeling of being nervous. Ask yourself: what is the writer really describing?
explain: In computing, jitter means small, unwanted wobbles in a signal or picture, or in the timing of data. A video call that keeps freezing may have jitter. Check the topic: if the sentence is about nerves, it is the everyday meaning; if it is about screens or connections, it is the computing meaning.
fact: The jitters (informal, a noun) means a nervous, shaky feeling, especially before something important.
fact: Jitter as a verb means to make small, quick, shaky movements.
fact: In computing, jitter means small, unwanted wobbles in a signal, a picture, or the timing of data.
fact: «Jitters» is linked with «worry» and «a bigger crash» in the context sentences, which points to a nervous feeling.
fact: Sleep, breakfast and water help a child focus, according to the text, while caffeine more often brings jitters.
exercise: «Two cans means twice the caffeine and more jitters and a bigger crash, not twice the fitness.» What does jitters mean here? | Sleepy, heavy feelings | Loud music from the cans | *Nervous, shaky feelings | Strong muscles and good health
exercise: The video call kept freezing because of jitter in the connection. What is jitter in this sentence? | A kind of game | *Small, unwanted wobbles in a signal | A cheerful song | A snack for the computer
exercise: Find and copy the word from «caffeine more often brings jitters and worry» that shows a feeling close to jitters. | Sleep | *Worry | Water | Breakfast
test: Before the spelling test, Sam had the jitters. What does the jitters mean? | Feeling very sleepy after lunch | Making quick, neat handwriting | A loud noise from the classroom | *A nervous, shaky feeling before something important
test: «Sleep, breakfast and water help a child focus; caffeine more often brings jitters and worry.» According to this sentence, what does caffeine more often bring? | Better focus | Fitness | *Jitters and worry | Sleep
exam: Mia says jitters is only a computer word. Is she right? | *No, jitters has an everyday meaning about nervous feelings, and jitter in computing is a different sense | No, jitters means a loud noise | Yes, because it is always a verb | Yes, only computers use the word jitters
